/-!
# Common residuals and fusion restrictions in §16.5

The residual construction proves the algebraic part of Notation 16.5.5 and
16.5.6(1)–(2) from cross-containment and local residual perfectness. The product
obstruction proves the deduction in 16.5.6(5) from its detector, normalizing
conjugator, and forbidden-projection inputs. All subgroups and Sylow witnesses
are actual subgroups of the ambient finite group.

This module does not yet assert Lemmas 16.5.2–10 under the chapter hypotheses.
Their Sylow alternatives, exceptional-group exclusions, residual normalizer,
two-central symmetry, and central-rank argument remain assembly obligations.
Any later application of 16.5.10 must retain its exclusion of groups of Lie
rank two over fields of order 2ⁿ with n > 1.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, pp.1195–1199.
-/
